# Copy this file to .env and fill in the values. .env is gitignored — never
# commit a real token.
#
# NETLIFY_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN
#   Used by the netlify-mcp server declared in .mcp.json, and by the Netlify
#   CLI if you use it locally. Create one at:
#     https://app.netlify.com/user/applications#personal-access-tokens
#   Scope it as narrowly as Netlify allows — whatever the token can do, any
#   tool holding it can do, including against production.
#
#   NOTE: a .env file is NOT read automatically by Claude Code. This file is
#   the canonical record of which variables exist and what they are for; the
#   copy Claude Code actually reads lives in .claude/settings.local.json
#   (gitignored). Keep the token in one of the two, not both.
NETLIFY_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN=
